  "rule": "Hollow single-colour frames of equal size are stacked in a left column, one background row apart. Small solid 4-connected shapes lie to the right of or below them. In the output every small shape is erased. Each frame receives n dots of its own colour on its middle row, at x1-2, x1-4, and so on stepping leftwards, where n is the number of small shapes of that frame's colour. Shapes whose colour has no frame just vanish.",
  "scope": "Constructive hollow-frame colour tallying: count separate same-colour shapes, erase all small shapes including distractors, then place dots on each frame middle row from right to left at two-column spacing. Varies frame dimensions, counts and transformed templates.",
  "constraints": [
    "All four canonical pairs reconstruct exactly.",
    "1180 unique independently decoded puzzles include 579 scenes with empty frames, 622 with a full-capacity frame, 800 with distractors and 992 with differently sized same-colour shapes.",
    "30 trials each exercise seven 3-row frames, zero framed counts plus distractors, full-capacity tallies, a non-square canvas, a single tall frame and a 27-column frame.",
    "Malformed scalar/unordered list controls and unhashable colour entries now reject with ValueError. Frame count documentation matches the 1..7 feasible range; six or seven require frame_height=3.",
    "A partially filled bordered shape is counted once, not mistaken for a hollow frame. Feasible dense 24-shape cases remain supported instead of being rejected by an unproven area heuristic.",
    "1000 independent archived-transform seeds pass; final critic proposals yield 27 successes and 7 expected rejections."
  ],
  "known_limitations": [
    "Native frames remain in a left stack with one-row gaps and shared odd dimensions; shapes come from a finite template catalogue under D4 transforms.",
    "Explicit larger solid or partially filled bordered shapes are allowed; only exact hollow rings are reserved as frames.",
    "Dense custom packing requests can exhaust bounded retries: two 27x9 frames with counts [12,12] succeed on four of five measured seeds and exhaust on one. This is not mislabelled geometrically impossible.",
    "Native count sampling caps the total framed shapes at 13; larger explicit requested counts are supported subject to capacity and placement."
  ],
