  "authored_scope": "Random path samples: background colour; frame count 2-5 (1 only on request or when a supplied height forces it); distinct frame colours; frame size (11x5 favoured; widths 7/9/13 and height 7 as synthetic extensions); origin 1..2 (0 only when needed to fit); grid size up to 30x30; per-frame counts 0..capacity; 0-2 distractor colours used 1-2 times each; shape templates under random rotation and reflection with random positions. Explicit options also allow odd frame widths up to 27, frame heights 3 and 9, and up to 9 frames. An explicit shapes list draws an exact scene, which validate() uses to rebuild all four fixtures. Deliberately not supported: frames of differing sizes, frames outside a single left column, irregular frame spacing, frames with non-background interiors, ring-shaped small shapes, shapes touching frames or each other, and counts above (W-2)//2 (the reference would truncate them).",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "Every small shape is 4-connected, is not a hollow rectangle ring, and keeps Chebyshev distance >= 2 from every frame cell and every other shape.",
    "Random shapes lie either right of the frame column (col >= left+fw+1) or entirely below the last frame.",
    "Frame colours are distinct and differ from the background. Distractor colours differ from both.",
    "The count for each frame colour is <= (frame_width-2)//2, so all dots fall strictly inside the frame.",
    "The background is the strict plurality colour of the input.",
    "At least one shape exists, so input != output.",
    "Booleans, floats, bare strings used as patterns, and other non-integer controls are rejected with ValueError."
  ],
  "semantic_review": {
    "status": "reviewed",
    "checks": [
      "All four canonical pairs reconstruct exactly.",
      "1180 unique independently decoded puzzles include 579 scenes with empty frames, 622 with a full-capacity frame, 800 with distractors and 992 with differently sized same-colour shapes.",
      "30 trials each exercise seven 3-row frames, zero framed counts plus distractors, full-capacity tallies, a non-square canvas, a single tall frame and a 27-column frame.",
      "Malformed scalar/unordered list controls and unhashable colour entries now reject with ValueError. Frame count documentation matches the 1..7 feasible range; six or seven require frame_height=3.",
      "A partially filled bordered shape is counted once, not mistaken for a hollow frame. Feasible dense 24-shape cases remain supported instead of being rejected by an unproven area heuristic.",
      "1000 independent archived-transform seeds pass; final critic proposals yield 27 successes and 7 expected rejections.",
      "1000 independent seeds 20000..20999; approved validation fixtures reconstructed exactly; canonical replay reported separately"
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "Native frames remain in a left stack with one-row gaps and shared odd dimensions; shapes come from a finite template catalogue under D4 transforms.",
      "Explicit larger solid or partially filled bordered shapes are allowed; only exact hollow rings are reserved as frames.",
      "Dense custom packing requests can exhaust bounded retries: two 27x9 frames with counts [12,12] succeed on four of five measured seeds and exhaust on one. This is not mislabelled geometrically impossible.",
      "Native count sampling caps the total framed shapes at 13; larger explicit requested counts are supported subject to capacity and placement."
    ]
  },
